SYSTEM pk: changelog, release and ship
ON git.design
REPORTS message
RUNS
    changelog
    release
    ship

PLACE settings ONE OUTSIDE
PLACE origin address ONE OUTSIDE
PLACE working branch SERIES LASTING
PLACE release branch SERIES LASTING
PLACE origin's working branch SERIES LASTING IN origin
PLACE origin's release branch SERIES LASTING IN origin
PLACE changelog file ONE LASTING IN working tree
PLACE version files ONE LASTING IN working tree
PLACE next version ONE RUN
PLACE commits since tag ONE RUN
PLACE section ONE RUN
PLACE message ONE REPORT
PLACE standard output ONE REPORT

FACT dry run
    SAYS --dry-run is given
FACT undo ONLY NOT in ship
    SAYS --undo is given
FACT nothing to release
    SAYS no commit since the last version tag is one the changelog lists
FACT no local version tag
    SAYS the repository has no version tag
FACT trunk flow
    SAYS release.branch is empty
FACT the last commit is a release commit ABOUT working branch
    SAYS HEAD carries a Release-Tag trailer
FACT the release is tagged ONLY the last commit is a release commit AND nothing to release AND NOT no local version tag
    SAYS the tag HEAD's Release-Tag trailer names exists on HEAD: that release has shipped
FACT the release tag is on another commit ONLY the last commit is a release commit AND NOT the release is tagged AND NOT no local version tag
    SAYS the tag HEAD's Release-Tag trailer names exists, on a commit other than HEAD
FACT a release is pending
    MEANS ALL
        the last commit is a release commit
        NOT the Release-Tag trailer is not a version
        NOT the release is tagged
        NOT the release tag is on another commit
    SAYS a Release-Tag trailer that reads as a version, on a commit whose tag does not exist yet
FAULT settings are invalid ABOUT settings
FAULT no branch is checked out ABOUT working branch
    SAYS HEAD is detached
FAULT the working branch is protected ABOUT working branch
    SAYS the branch is one guard.branches lists
FAULT the working branch is not on origin ABOUT working branch
FAULT the working branch is behind origin ABOUT working branch
    SAYS origin's tip of the branch is not in the branch's history: changelog reads it with no fetch and makes no check; release reads it after fetching
FACT origin names no default branch ONLY trunk flow
    SAYS origin advertises no HEAD, so the default-branch check cannot run
FAULT the branch is not the default ABOUT working branch ONLY trunk flow AND NOT origin names no default branch
FACT a tag does not name a version ABOUT tags
    SAYS the repository has a tag whose name is not a version
FAULT the changelog file cannot be read ABOUT changelog file
FAULT a version file has no version field ABOUT version files
FACT origin has no address ABOUT origin address
    SAYS origin's URL gives no web address; a local path gives a link made from the path
FAULT the last version tag is not in the branch's history
FAULT the postVersion command fails
FAULT the preCommit command fails
FAULT the preRelease command fails
FAULT the prePush command fails
FAULT the --bump value is not a level
FAULT an --exclude entry matches no commit
FAULT not a git repository
    SAYS no git repository encloses the project directory
FAULT settings are missing ABOUT settings
    SAYS there is no .pk.json
FAULT the working branch is the release branch ABOUT working branch ONLY NOT trunk flow
    SAYS merge flow, and the branch checked out is release.branch
FAULT the Release-Tag trailer is not a version ABOUT working branch ONLY the last commit is a release commit
    SAYS HEAD's Release-Tag trailer does not name a version
FACT every commit is excluded ONLY NOT nothing to release
    SAYS no conventional commit remains after --exclude
FACT no commit is in a visible section ONLY NOT nothing to release
    SAYS every commit's type is hidden or has no section
FACT the release branch is not on origin ONLY NOT trunk flow
    SAYS origin has no release.branch
FAULT the release branch does not exist ONLY NOT trunk flow AND the release branch is not on origin
    SAYS release.branch is neither a local branch nor on origin
FAULT origin's release branch is not in the working branch's history ABOUT origin's release branch ONLY NOT trunk flow AND NOT the release branch is not on origin
    SAYS after a fetch of the release branch, origin's tip of it is not in the working branch's history

SEQ changelog
    load settings
    CHOOSE
        WHEN undo
            undo
        OTHERWISE
            make changelog

ACTION undo
    USES reset to the commit before
        WITH the branch = working branch
    MAKES NOT the last commit is a release commit
    REHEARSAL dry run
    REFUSE WHEN working branch is held elsewhere
        SAYS --undo refuses a commit that is pushed, tagged or merged
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestUndoRefusesACommitSomethingElseHolds
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
    REFUSE WHEN NOT the last commit is a release commit
    REFUSE WHEN the Release-Tag trailer is not a version
    ACCEPT
        WHEN ANY
            the branch is not the default
            no branch is checked out
            the working branch is protected
            the working branch is not on origin
            the working branch is behind origin
        BECAUSE undo removes only a commit that nothing else holds, so the branch it is on does not matter
    SAYS --undo unwinds the release commit and restores the changelog file and the version files

SEQ make changelog
    branch checks
    fetch the tags WHEN no local version tag
    measure the commits
    CHOOSE
        WHEN nothing to release
            say nothing to release
        OTHERWISE
            SEQ
                infer version
                CHOOSE
                    WHEN every commit is excluded
                        say nothing to release
                    OTHERWISE
                        SEQ
                            pending release check
                            CHOOSE
                                WHEN no commit is in a visible section
                                    say nothing to release
                                OTHERWISE
                                    SEQ
                                        build section
                                        CHOOSE
                                            WHEN dry run
                                                print section
                                            OTHERWISE
                                                write release

ACTION branch checks
    READS
        settings
        working tree
        working branch
        origin
    ACCEPT WHEN the working branch is behind origin
        BECAUSE changelog makes no check for it; release refuses it before tagging
    REFUSE WHEN NOT dry run AND (working tree holds what is kept nowhere OR no branch is checked out)
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestRefusals
    REFUSE WHEN the working branch is protected OR the working branch is not on origin OR origin does not answer
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestRefusals
    REFUSE WHEN the branch is not the default
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestTrunkFlowRefusesNonDefaultBranch
    ACCEPT WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere OR no branch is checked out
        BECAUSE a dry run writes nothing, so it may read the commits from anywhere
    ACCEPT WHEN origin names no default branch
        BECAUSE the check cannot run, and changelog goes on without saying so

ACTION fetch the tags
    USES fetch tags
    LATER STANDS
    ACCEPT WHEN origin does not answer
        BECAUSE the fetch fails, the ls-remote of origin's tags fails too, and the run goes on as a first release without a word
    FAIL WHEN tags already has the member
        SAYS the fetch exits 1 after creating the other tags; ls-remote finds origin's tags, and pk refuses and says to fetch them
    ACCEPT WHEN tags is given a key twice
        BECAUSE git's reason stands: a remote holds one tag of each name.
    SAYS with no local tags, changelog fetches origin's tags first and measures from the latest
    BECAUSE the tags fetched are origin's, and a later run would fetch them again

ACTION infer version
    READS commits since tag
    CREATE next version
    TELL WHEN an --exclude entry matches no commit
    REFUSE WHEN the --bump value is not a level AND NOT every commit is excluded
    ACCEPT WHEN the --bump value is not a level
        BECAUSE when every commit is excluded the run says nothing to release before it reads --bump

ACTION pending release check WHEN NOT dry run
    READS working branch
    ACCEPT WHEN the Release-Tag trailer is not a version
        BECAUSE the check refuses only a trailer it can read as a version
    REFUSE WHEN the last commit is a release commit

ACTION say nothing to release
    CREATE message

ACTION build section
    READS
        settings
        commits since tag
        next version
    CREATE section

ACTION print section
    READS section
    CREATE standard output

SEQ write release
    stamp versions
    postVersion hook
    write section
    preCommit hook
    commit the release

ACTION stamp versions
    READS
        settings
        next version
        version files
    REPLACE version files
        LATER UNDONE
        SAYS when a version file or a hook fails, nothing is committed and the tree goes back to how the run found it
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestARefusedReleasePutsTheWholeTreeBack
    REFUSE WHEN a version file has no version field

ACTION postVersion hook
    READS
        settings
        next version
    REFUSE WHEN the postVersion command fails
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestFailingHookAborts

ACTION write section
    READS
        section
        changelog file
        commits since tag
        next version
        origin address
    REPLACE changelog file
        LATER UNDONE
    REFUSE WHEN the changelog file cannot be read
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestAChangelogThatIsThereMustBeReadable
    ACCEPT WHEN origin has no address
        BECAUSE the section is written with no link, and changelog says nothing

ACTION preCommit hook
    READS
        settings
        next version
    REFUSE WHEN the preCommit command fails

ACTION commit the release
    USES commit
        WITH the branch = working branch
    MAKES the last commit is a release commit
    LATER UNDONE
    REFUSE WHEN the commit cannot be made
    SAYS pk ship runs changelog and then release, and when the release half fails it undoes the changelog commit it made
    HOLD internal/ship/ship_test.go TestFailedReleaseUndoesTheChangelogCommit

SEQ release
    read the current branch
    load settings
    read the pending release
    check the branch on origin
    fetch the working branch
    fetch the release branch WHEN NOT trunk flow AND NOT the release branch is not on origin
    pre-flight
    merge WHEN NOT trunk flow
    preRelease hook
    tag the release WHEN NOT dry run
    prePush hook WHEN NOT dry run
    CHOOSE WHEN NOT dry run
        WHEN trunk flow
            push in trunk flow
        OTHERWISE
            push in merge flow
    switch back WHEN NOT dry run AND NOT trunk flow
    push the working branch WHEN NOT dry run AND NOT trunk flow
    SAYS in trunk flow there is no merge: the release tags and pushes the default branch

ACTION fetch the working branch
    USES fetch the branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    LATER STANDS
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    ACCEPT WHEN remote-tracking branch holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE pre-flight fetches, which brings it up to date
    BECAUSE a remote-tracking branch is a copy of origin's branch, and the next fetch makes it again

ACTION pre-flight
    READS
        working branch
        remote-tracking branch
        release branch
        tags
    REFUSE
        WHEN ANY
            the working branch is behind origin
            the release branch does not exist
            origin's release branch is not in the working branch's history
            the last version tag is not in the branch's history
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestRefusals
    TELL WHEN origin names no default branch
        SAYS the run says the default-branch check could not run, and goes on

SEQ merge
    ACTION switch to the release branch
        USES switch
            WITH the branch = release branch
        LATER UNDONE
        REHEARSAL dry run
        REFUSE WHEN the switch fails
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestRejectedPushRollsEverythingBack
    ACTION fast-forward the release branch
        USES fast-forward
            WITH the branch = release branch
            WITH the other branch = working branch
        LATER UNDONE
        REHEARSAL dry run
        REFUSE WHEN the branch cannot be fast-forwarded
            HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestDivergedReleaseBranchRefused
    SAYS a release dry run rehearses the merge against origin's release branch when there is no local one
    SAYS a failure after tagging rolls back: the local tag is deleted, the merge is reset, and the working branch is checked out

ACTION preRelease hook
    READS
        settings
        working branch
    REFUSE WHEN the preRelease command fails

ACTION tag the release
    USES tag
        WITH the branch = working branch
    LATER UNDONE
    REFUSE WHEN the tag cannot be created
    ACCEPT WHEN tags already has the member
        BECAUSE read the pending release refuses a tag already made, before the tag

ACTION prePush hook
    READS
        settings
        working branch
    REFUSE WHEN the prePush command fails
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestFailingPrePushCleansUp

ACTION push in trunk flow
    USES push the branch and the tag
        WITH the branch = working branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    LATER STANDS
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer OR origin rejects the push OR (origin's tags already has the member AND NOT origin's tag names the commit pushed)
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestRejectedPushRollsEverythingBack
    ACCEPT WHEN origin's tags already has the member AND origin's tag names the commit pushed
        BECAUSE origin already has the tag on the commit the release pushes, so git takes the push
    BECAUSE once the branch and the tag are on origin the release stands

ACTION push in merge flow
    USES push the branch and the tag
        WITH the branch = release branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's release branch
    LATER STANDS
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer OR origin rejects the push OR (origin's tags already has the member AND NOT origin's tag names the commit pushed)
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestRejectedPushRollsEverythingBack
    ACCEPT WHEN origin's tags already has the member AND origin's tag names the commit pushed
        BECAUSE origin already has the tag on the commit the release pushes, so git takes the push
    SAYS the release branch and the tag are pushed together
    BECAUSE once the release branch and the tag are on origin the release stands

ACTION switch back
    USES switch
        WITH the branch = working branch
    WARN WHEN the switch fails
        SAYS once the release branch and the tag are on origin the release stands: a failure to switch back or to push the working branch is a warning

ACTION push the working branch
    USES push the branch
        WITH the branch = working branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's working branch
    WARN WHEN origin does not answer OR origin rejects the push

CHOOSE ship
    WHEN a release is pending
        release
    OTHERWISE
        SEQ
            changelog
            CHOOSE
                WHEN dry run
                    say release rehearses later
                WHEN the last commit is a release commit
                    release
                OTHERWISE
                    NOTHING
    SAYS a release already pending is resumed at release; after a changelog that made no release commit, ship stops

ACTION load settings
    READS settings
    REFUSE WHEN not a git repository
    REFUSE WHEN settings are missing
        SAYS pk names pk init
    REFUSE WHEN settings are invalid
        SAYS An unknown key or a value outside these fails the whole file when it loads, with a message naming the key: pk commands exit 2

ACTION measure the commits
    READS
        tags
        working branch
    CREATE commits since tag
    REFUSE WHEN the last version tag is not in the branch's history
        HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestTagOutsideHistoryIsRefused
    SAYS the latest version tag and the commits since it; after a fetch of the tags, measured again

ACTION read the current branch
    READS working branch
    REFUSE WHEN not a git repository
    REFUSE WHEN no branch is checked out

ACTION read the pending release
    READS
        settings
        working branch
        tags
    REFUSE WHEN the working branch is the release branch
    REFUSE
        WHEN ANY
            NOT the last commit is a release commit
            the Release-Tag trailer is not a version
            the release is tagged
            the release tag is on another commit
            tags already has the member
        SAYS no trailer, a trailer that is not a version, or its tag already made, on HEAD or another commit

ACTION check the branch on origin
    READS
        working tree
        working branch
        origin's working branch
    REFUSE WHEN working tree holds what is kept nowhere
    REFUSE WHEN the branch is not the default AND NOT origin names no default branch
        HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestTrunkFlowRefusesNonDefaultBranch
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer OR the working branch is not on origin

ACTION fetch the release branch
    USES fetch the branch
        WITH origin's branch = origin's release branch
    LATER STANDS
    REFUSE WHEN origin does not answer
    ACCEPT WHEN remote-tracking branch holds what is kept nowhere
        BECAUSE a remote-tracking branch is a copy of origin's branch, and the next fetch makes it again
    SAYS the code fetches it after the behind check and the check that the release branch exists; the language has one remote-tracking branch, so the order plays the same
    BECAUSE what pre-flight fetched from origin stays

ACTION say release rehearses later
    CREATE message
    SAYS a dry changelog makes no release commit, so the release half has nothing to rehearse; ship says so and stops

EXPECT changelog with --dry-run writes nothing
    IN changelog
    WHEN dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        working tree
        tags
        origin
        remote-tracking branch
        release branch
        working branch
    SAYS changelog with --dry-run prints the section to standard output and writes nothing
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestDryRunPrintsSectionToStdout

EXPECT --undo with --dry-run changes nothing
    IN changelog
    WHEN undo AND dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        working tree
        tags
        origin
        remote-tracking branch
        release branch
        working branch
    SAYS --undo with --dry-run makes the same checks and changes nothing
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestUndoWithDryRunChangesNothing

EXPECT a release dry run merges nothing, tags nothing and pushes nothing
    IN release
    WHEN dry run
    NEVER CHANGES
        release branch
        working tree
        tags
        origin
    SAYS release with --dry-run merges nothing, tags nothing and pushes nothing
    HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestDryRunTouchesNothing

EXPECT a release ends with the tag and the branches on origin
    IN release
    WHEN NOT dry run
    ON SUCCESS
    ENDS origin CHANGED
    ENDS tags CREATED
    SAYS a release ends on the working branch, with the tag, the release branch and the working branch all on origin
    HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestMergeFlowReleases

EXPECT preRelease runs before the tag exists
    IN release
    BEFORE preRelease hook PLACE tags IS UNTOUCHED
    SAYS preRelease runs before the tag exists, and prePush runs with the tag in existence
    HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestHooks

EXPECT prePush runs with the tag in existence
    IN release
    BEFORE prePush hook PLACE tags IS CREATED
    HOLD internal/release/release_test.go TestHooks

RULE a breaking change bumps major, a feat bumps minor, and anything else bumps patch
    ABOUT infer version
    SAYS a breaking change bumps major, a feat bumps minor, and anything else bumps patch
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestBumpInference

RULE --bump overrides the inferred version, and the run names the override
    ABOUT infer version
    SAYS --bump overrides the inferred version, and the run names the override
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestBumpOverrideAndValidation

RULE --exclude drops commits before the version is inferred
    ABOUT infer version
    SAYS --exclude drops commits before the version is inferred
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestExcludeAffectsBump

RULE with no version tag, the first release covers the whole history
    ABOUT infer version
    SAYS with no version tag, the first release covers the whole history
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestFirstReleaseCoversAllHistory

RULE a preRelease hook that commits produces a commit the tag then covers
    ABOUT preRelease hook
    SAYS a preRelease hook that commits produces a commit the tag then covers

RULE version inference passes over a tag that is not a version, and counts a pre-release tag as the latest version
    ABOUT infer version
    WHEN a tag does not name a version
    HOLD internal/changelog/changelog_test.go TestANonVersionTagIsNotARelease
